Use a simple Python script (opencv or numpy) to read the map.png heightmap.
Apply a gradient filter (like Sobel operators) to detect steep slopes (craters, rocks).
Threshold the gradient image: steep slopes = occupied space (black), flat slopes = free space (white), out of boundary/unseen = grey.
Save the thresholded image as a .pgm file and write a corresponding .yaml file defining the resolution (meters/pixel) matching your physical yard bounds.
